ZIG-MAN(7)						    Zig Manual						       ZIG-MAN(7)

NAME
       zig-man - man pages for the Zig programming language

DESCRIPTION
       zig-man is a collection of manual pages for the Zig programming language.

INSTALL
	   make install

       Default prefix is /usr/local. Override with PREFIX=/path. Stage with DESTDIR=/path. Remove with make uninstall.

READ
	   man 7 zig-variables
	   man 1 zig

       Read from source without installing:
	   man -l man/man7/zig-variables.7

STRUCTURE
	   man/man1/   commands
	   man/man3/   library reference
	   man/man5/   file formats
	   man/man7/   topic overviews

DEVELOPMENT
   Preview
	   make preview FILE=man/man7/zig-variables.7
	   make watch	FILE=man/man7/zig-variables.7

   Lint and check
	   make lint
	   make check
	   make check-strict

   Render
	   make html	# build/html/
	   make pdf	# build/pdf/
	   make txt	# build/txt/

   Metadata
	   make format-header
	   make format-footer
	   make format

       The commit hook in .githooks/pre-commit updates the .TH date automatically. Enable it with:
	   make install-hooks

WRITING PAGES
       Files are named name.section. The first line is .TH:
	   .TH ZIG-VARIABLES 7 "2026-01-01" "Zig 0.17.0" "Zig Manual"

       Every page ends with three sections in this order:
	   .SH AUTHORS
	   .SH COPYRIGHT
	   .SH SOURCE

       Run make format to fill these in, or enable the commit hook.

CONTRIBUTING
       Pull requests welcome. Run make lint and make check before opening a pull request.

